It's a relex in the broad sense of a one-to-one correspondence between the
parts of words.

The first syllable of a word is its semantic classifier, which for lujvo is
usually the same as for the main word of the tanru it's based on.

I changed the lujvo rules and the morphology (phonology too, but that
didn't show in the example). Whether it's still self-segregating or not, I
don't know (and don't much care).

It helped alleviate my frustration with Lojban gismu.

stevo


